!projects/*/exports/models/*.stl

# The commons repo carries its own gitlinks for the six third-party OpenSCAD
# libraries (projects/libs/*), pinned at the SAME commits as the platform's
# top-level libs/ — they exist so `y4d-spec check --render` resolves OpenSCAD
# cartridges inside the commons repo standalone. A `submodules: recursive`
# checkout materialises them, and `COPY projects/` would then put a second
# ~330 MB copy of BOSL2/NopSCADlib/dotSCAD/MCAD/Round-Anything/threads-scad
# into the image beside `COPY libs/`. Nothing resolves `projects/libs`: the
# OpenSCAD search path is `/libs` (config.py, and VIRTUAL_OPENSCADPATH in the
# Studio worker), so excluding it keeps the image identical to before the
# commons gained these gitlinks.
projects/libs/
coverage/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.serena/
.playwright-mcp/
.dev-pids/
.venv/
venv/
dist/
*.log
.env
.env.local
